    "memoEntities": {
      "2rGgnXf5x3S_8_WaMqcL1": {
        "id": "2rGgnXf5x3S_8_WaMqcL1",
        "value": "One Property can have many Reviews (multiple users review it)\nOne Review is about one Property only\nSo it's 1:M — Property (1) to Review (M).\n\nAnd for User - Review?\nOne User can write many Reviews\nOne Review is written by one User",
        "ui": {
          "x": 1095.129,
          "y": 764.0985,
          "zIndex": 370,
          "width": 368,
          "height": 110,
          "color": ""
        },
        "meta": {
          "updateAt": 1771113729968,
          "createAt": 1771110953743
        }
      },
      "PuwDBQ8DFyOS585cqXRA5": {
        "id": "PuwDBQ8DFyOS585cqXRA5",
        "value": " M:N cannot exist in the relational model directly. The lecturer said the rule: create a new table with both PKs as FKs. That new table automatically sits in the middle with two 1:M relationships\n\n\nConceptual (ERD):\n    Property ──(M)────── has ──────(N)── Facility\n\n\nLogical (Tables):\n    Property ──(1)── has ──(M)── Property_Facility ──(M)── has ──(1)── Facility",
        "ui": {
          "x": 1375.6157,
          "y": 444.4769,
          "zIndex": 421,
          "width": 556,
          "height": 160,
          "color": ""
        },
        "meta": {
          "updateAt": 1771113759564,
          "createAt": 1771111464654
        }
      },
      "YJIStDkoRUoqeXUkNWmKx": {
        "id": "YJIStDkoRUoqeXUkNWmKx",
        "value": "Facilities = \"either you have it or you don't\" (presence-based)\nConstraints = \"every property must say yes or no\" (value-based)",
        "ui": {
          "x": 1372.1517,
          "y": 280.7013,
          "zIndex": 804,
          "width": 554,
          "height": 100,
          "color": ""
        },
        "meta": {
          "updateAt": 1771115899814,
          "createAt": 1771115886112
        }
      }
    }
  }
